# Signs cookies and derives verification/state tokens; generate a long random value (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`) and set it on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`, never commit the real value.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# Public origin of the site that owns the Better Auth session (e.g. https://admin.illith.com in production); set on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Regenerating the Better Auth schema requires both variables to be present in the
# shell, because convex/betterAuth/auth.ts constructs a real auth instance for the
# generator to introspect, and createAuth refuses to build one without them.
# Throwaway values are fine — they are never persisted and never leave your shell:
#
#   cd packages/backend/convex/betterAuth
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=dev SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000 \
#     corepack pnpm@10 dlx auth@1.6.17 generate --y
#
# The guard lives in createAuth deliberately: it is the only place betterAuth() is
# constructed, so a missing secret can never fall back to the library's
# publicly-known default.
